    "turn_text": "Do not miss U.S. Representative Chip Roy. He's going to be honored about eight or nine minutes. Make sure you stick around for that. We're going to break down why he's on the campaign trail with Ron DeSantis. We're going to also talk about what we do about the border, what we do about the spending, what we do about the budget is Mike Johnson doing all that he thought Mike Johnson would do. Interesting conversation. Now he does. He goes into sort of campaign mode about DeSantis. And I make it clear, a lot of what you just said I can disagree with. But I'm not going to campaign for Trump. I'm not going to debate you on it. I want to have you want to talk about what's going on in government and so on. We do talk about Nikki Haley. Why would Nikki Haley come out the other night and say that thing? By the way, a lot of you have contacted me. A lot of you have said Nikki Haley was talking about between her and DeSantis, not including Trump. I disagree. Nikki Haley came out the other night to say it's between her and Trump. And in fact, she proves that point by turning down the debate with DeSantis that was coming up on ABC soon. So Nikki Haley, for some reason in third place, thinks that she can say it's between her and Trump when again, there was a person in between. Okay. So, interesting conversation with Chip. Again, he gets into campaign mode. My job is not to debate him. I think he's wrong about some of the stuff he says about Trump, and I let him know that, but then we move on. So make sure you stick around. Chip is somebody who is big time about closed the border. Big time about stopping the spending just on everything. And the border is a very, very important thing. Especially for those of us here in Texas, Chip is a representative from Texas. We talk a lot about that. But this story just came in, which I find to be interesting. The Biden administration has been suing about the floating barrier that Texas put in the Rio Grande to stop people from